      "id": "tech-https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50204125",
      "title": "Median product \"lifespan\" has fallen from ~4y down to ~1.5y",
      "description": "The \"product graveyard\" of SaaSHub has been tracking the status (and lifespan) of hundreds of thousands of products. It's been hovering around 4y for quite some time. However, there's a sharp decline in 2026 leading to about 1.5y these days. https://www.saashub.com/product-graveyard That's a huge drop. And, it matches my \"human\" observations. A lot of products are being vibe coded, released, and soon after that abandoned. It's become too cheap to produce software. So, a lot of people have been experimenting for 'free' with their ideas - only to find out that they weren't viable... or that they couldn't bring customers in. Distribution and marketing have become much more important than before - within the context that everyone can build \"features\" for free.Anyhow, I expect this trend of shortening product lifespan to continue even further down. Or maybe, at some point people will realised that there are no users for their products as every user can \"build\" their own and custom product. Leaving us with a dozen huge platforms that host and help you build those apps. Until then - it's a crazy gold rush and a lot of makers are abandoning their empty buckets.\n\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50204125\nPoints: 15\n# Comments: 3",
      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50204125",
